From ec6cd5ec323437c20ac13463f56fb6be37e27af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Meyer <katexochen0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:37:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bldr: drop the 0x10000 offset from the SIPI GDT load

The 16-bit SIPI entry code loads the GDT with

    lgdtl %cs:0x10000 + gdt_desc - base_entry

base_entry is linked at 0x10000, so the operand evaluates to 0x10008,
the linear address of gdt_desc. In 16-bit mode the displacement field is
16 bits wide though, and LLVM up to 22 silently truncated the value to
0x0008, which is what the instruction needs: after the SIPI, %cs has a
base of 0x10000, so the displacement must be the offset of gdt_desc
inside the startup page.

LLVM 23 rejects the truncation instead:

    error: value of 65544 is too large for field of 2 bytes

which breaks the build with Rust 1.99 as shipped by Fedora rawhide.
Use the offset directly. The encoding (2e 66 0f 01 16 08 00) is
identical to what older LLVM produced, so the generated code does not
change.

Signed-off-by: Paul Meyer <katexochen0@gmail.com>
---
 boot/bldr/src/main.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/boot/bldr/src/main.rs b/boot/bldr/src/main.rs
index 8a90087..98a9b9e 100644
--- a/boot/bldr/src/main.rs
+++ b/boot/bldr/src/main.rs
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ global_asm!(
         movl %cr0, %eax
         orl ${CR0_PE}, %eax // enable protected mode
         movl %eax, %cr0
-        lgdtl %cs:0x10000 + gdt_desc - base_entry
+        lgdtl %cs:gdt_desc - base_entry
         ljmpl $8, $startup_ap
 
         .code32
-- 
2.56.0

